", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JzNLuhaDfb5mZTUkFUtRe6", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 385078, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JzNLuhaDfb5mZTUkFUtRe6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 389446, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened a pull request asking alex to review it.\n\n- **The bug:** in `src/money.py`, `round_money` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding. For example, 2.665 became 2.67, but `tests/test_money.py` expects 2.66.\n- **The fix:** on branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986), I changed it to use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 against main, with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool doesn't recognise that ID. The fix is based on the docstring and the test, which agree. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012sXxSUeCrBkaiuyb7puE46", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VgmHUoXYt7y2fprDCvkbe8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01L9HxtYNn9Cj7RGS4jgVNBG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": 